@@ -23,4 +23,11 @@ Resolve the immutable source revision before rendering. The cache key includes c
 
 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The worker uses 2Q eviction to protect reused comparison sheets during sequential screenings. The cache is split into two queues, Q1 and Q2, each with a size budget that together sum to 12 GiB. First access to a preview places it in Q1 as a FIFO queue. A second access promotes the entry from Q1 to Q2, which is also FIFO. Eviction targets Q1 first; when Q1 is empty, eviction targets Q2. Replacement bookkeeping, queue membership, and size accounting remain private to the preview worker. The external interface, render queue concurrency, and disk budget are unchanged.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Eviction policy | 2Q with separate first-use and reused queues | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | 2Q protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from one-off screening scans while keeping external contracts unchanged. Extra bookkeeping is acceptable to preserve the working set. |
+| Queue size split | 6 GiB Q1 / 6 GiB Q2, configurable | 50/50 split is the starting point; tuning allowed later | Equal split provides a balanced initial protection for first-use scans and reused sheets; can be adjusted based on observed workloads without changing the interface. |
diff --git a/docs/intent/previews/previews-specs.md b/docs/intent/previews/previews-specs.md
